    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nWhen deleting the last argument of an argument list, the space character before the closing list character is deleted also.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.7.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nWith this argument list : `{ a, b }` (`^` is cursor position, `daa` is keymap for delete argument) :\r\n\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n```\r\n{ a, b } ==daa==> { a } // OK, space kept after 'a'\r\n     ^\r\n```\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n```\r\n{ a, b } ==daa==> { a} // KO, no space after 'a'\r\n     ^\r\n```",
    "closed_at": "2022-08-11T17:16:58Z",
