        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> - This, of course, should also be the case for the first argument?\r\n\r\nYes, the first argument should be processed the same way : `{ a, b }` => `{ b }`. \r\n\r\n> - If there is more than one space, would you expect to ignore all of them?\r\n\r\nI think it's probably better, yes.\r\n\r\n> - Would you also expect `vaa` to ignore whitespace?\r\n\r\nYes\r\n\r\nI used Targets.vim previously and it has the following behavior:\r\n- spaces before the first argument are ignored\r\n- spaces after the last argument are ignored\r\n- spaces between arguments are taken into account\r\n\r\nExamples:\r\n\r\n```\r\n{    a,    b    } ==daa==> {    b    }\r\n     ^\r\n\r\n{    a,    b    } ==daa==> {    a    }\r\n           ^\r\n\r\n{    a,    b    } ==vaa==> {    a,    b    }\r\n     ^                          ------       // selection\r\n\r\n{    a,    b    } ==vaa==> {    a,    b    }\r\n           ^                     ------      // selection\r\n```",
