        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Hi. Also coming from targets.vim and I noticed that this behaviour is different:\r\n\r\nExpected behaviour:\r\n```\r\n{    a,    b    } ==vaa==> {    a,    b    }\r\n     ^                          ------       // selection\r\n```\r\n\r\nBehaviour in mini.ai:\r\n```\r\n{    a,    b    } ==vaa==> {    a,    b    }\r\n     ^                          --           // selection\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo deleting the first argument via `daa` in\r\n```\r\nitems = append(items, item)\r\n```\r\nleads to\r\n```\r\nitems = append( item)\r\n```\r\nhaving this would make more sense IMO:\r\n```\r\nitems = append(item)\r\n```",
