        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "\r\n\r\n\r\n> ...\r\n> leads to\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> items = append( item)\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> having this would make more sense IMO:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> items = append(item)\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nI kind of both agree and disagree. To me, when designing this, an argument is \"a region inside balanced bracket between allowed not excluded separators\". An `a` version here is an argument with corresponding separator. As there should be symmetry breaking in terms of whitespace, this is a behavior ended up in final version. But I do agree that it is annoying sometimes.\r\n\r\nI think there was an attempt to fix this, but I could come up only with such complicated approaches, that I decided to apply KISS here and endure suffering.",
