            "body": "> FYI: I am now using the following custom solution:\r\n> ...\r\n\r\nWoah, this is **the dedication** right here! Very nice, if it is working for you!\r\nI am somewhat relieved that this code can be processed by someone other than myself :)\r\n\r\n> One downside is when being on a whitespace there are 2 possible arguments which can cover the cursor and I cannot specify the right one (or \"best\"). But otherwise it feels natural to me.\r\n\r\nYeah, I don't think that making it default is good. Maybe in an option somehow?\r\nIf you'll have more free time, could you, please, make it in a patch against current 'lua/mini/ai.lua'? I started trying to align them, but there seems to be quite a few minor differences that makes it difficult without knowing which parts actually changed.",
